From fc26d1ca5dcf87d7f54f04ec2813542d9781b0e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:35:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [fold] give folded instances the location of their property

With -meta-fold, an instance is a call to the generated predicate,
built by create_call with Logic_const.papp and no location, so it gets
the kernel's generated location. The assertion then shows up as
"generated by Frama-C kernel" in WP goals and in the report, and
E-ACSL reports its failure at "<unknown>:0", while the same property
unfolded keeps the location of the meta property. The oracle of
meta-wp/typing.c in the fold config recorded this.

The call now takes the location of the instance it stands for.

The wrappers added around an instance had the same defect, folded or
not: the implication from the assumes of a callee's behavior (post) and
the \forall from -meta-quantify-range (post_fold), in the writing and
reading contexts, were built with the default location. They now keep
the location of the predicate they wrap.

Only locations change. New test tests/meta/fold_location.c checks all
three paths (folded calls, behavior assumes and -meta-quantify-range in
both writing and reading contexts) with -report in both the default and
fold configurations, and tests/meta-wp/oracle_fold/typing.0.res.oracle
is updated accordingly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
